Kickolé realistic assets
========================

kickole_player_v4.glb, kickole_player_v4_lod1.glb,
kickole_player_v4_female.glb and kickole_player_v4_female_lod1.glb
---------------------------------------------------------------------
These four files are optimised game models derived from two realistic
footballers bought on Fab.

  Licence:     Fab Standard License, Personal tier
  Licensee:    Rob Stancombe t/a IQ Apps Group
  Artist:      artistofthemonth
  Male source: the 21,071-triangle model with the Godot humanoid rig
               (84 bones in the download; reduced to the game contract)
  Female source: the 29,085-triangle model with the normal FBX rig

The optimised GLBs may ship inside the Kickolé app and the web build.
The raw purchased source (zips, FBX, blend, and the unpacked textures)
must not be redistributed and is not in this repository.

Rebuild with `npm run build:player`. The script expects the download at
`FAB_PLAYER_SRC` (default `/cursor/stores/bot/kickole-fab-models`),
containing `source_4.zip` (male) and `source.zip` (female). It writes only
the four GLBs above. Do not commit the Fab download.

Both bodies share the skeleton and clip contract in `docs/CHARACTER_GLB.md`.
Fingers, twist bones and face bones are merged into at most 20 joints.
The clips (Idle, KickLeft, KickRight, Miss, Celebrate) are original and
sampled from the game pose. Kit colours and the chest number are applied
at runtime. No club, league or real-player likeness is included. Both
bodies are free in the game.

Court and lighting textures
---------------------------
tools/street-sources/asphalt_*.jpg
  Poly Haven asphalt_02, 1K, CC0. Build input, not shipped.
  https://polyhaven.com/a/asphalt_02

tools/street-sources/concrete_*.jpg
  Poly Haven concrete_wall_001, 1K, CC0. Build input, not shipped.
  https://polyhaven.com/a/concrete_wall_001

tools/street-sources/wall_graffiti.jpg
  Earlier mural on the concrete photograph. The shipped wall is the
  KTX2 map below. The photograph remains CC0. The mural is original.

public/textures/sunflowers_puresky_1k.hdr
  Poly Haven sunflowers_puresky, 1K, CC0.
  https://polyhaven.com/a/sunflowers_puresky
  Warm sunny daytime sky and image-based light for the street court.
  It stays an RGBE .hdr because the PMREM pass needs the high range.
  Sampled surface textures are KTX2 instead.

public/textures/street/*.ktx2
  Court, wall and concrete maps are KTX2 (ETC1S colour and roughness,
  UASTC normals) built by tools/build_street_court.ts.
  Colour sources:
    Poly Haven asphalt_02, CC0. https://polyhaven.com/a/asphalt_02
    Poly Haven concrete_wall_001, CC0. https://polyhaven.com/a/concrete_wall_001
    Poly Haven concrete_floor_damaged_01, CC0.
    https://polyhaven.com/a/concrete_floor_damaged_01
  Lines, wear, the mural and the side-wall tag are original paint on
  those photographs. The damaged-floor photographs are fetched when the
  textures are rebuilt and are not stored as extra JPEGs.

public/models/environment/street/*.glb
  Original fence, lamp and spectator meshes, EXT_meshopt_compression.
  No downloaded character models. Rebuild with npm run build:street.

Quaternius sources still in this folder
---------------------------------------
kickole_player_v2.glb and kickole_player_v3.glb are derived from the
Quaternius Universal Base Characters (Standard), CC0 1.0 Universal.
They are not the default runtime character. See LICENSE.txt.
